Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2G): expand virtual mixed-
filament IDs into their physical components when collecting
painting_extruders in Print::apply.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/PrintApply.cpp` `append_mixed_component_extruders`
+ caller.

Why this matters (correctness fix for painted virtual filaments):

When the user paints triangles with a virtual mixed-filament state
ID (id > num_physical), our v2.3.2 code at PrintApply.cpp:1772 just
`painting_extruders.emplace_back(state_idx)`. Downstream the
per-physical-extruder buffer allocations don't cover the actual
physical(s) the resolver will pick per layer — so painted regions
for virtual filaments silently print on T0 only, ignoring the
LayerCycle / Pointillisme / pattern resolution.

This patch adds two helpers:

- `append_unique_painted_extruder` — dedupes + clamps to physical
  range.
- `append_mixed_component_extruders` — when state_id is virtual,
  emplaces component_a + component_b + every digit in
  gradient_component_ids + every distinct digit in manual_pattern.

The caller at the `used_facet_states` walk emplaces the literal
state_idx (preserves prior behavior) AND calls the new helper to
expand virtual rows into physicals. Physical IDs short-circuit
inside the helper.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (4/4 objects,
0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug (full APK assembled).

Hard dependencies:
  - patch 0015 (MixedFilamentManager + MixedFilament definitions)
  - patch 0017 (m_mixed_filament_mgr member on Print)

Companion to:
  - 0032 (LayerRegion virtual filament resolution — runs per-layer)
  - 0034 (PrintRegion infill-filament-override — runs per-preset)

This patch handles paint-state-driven expansion (mm_segmentation
facets), the missing leg of the trio.

